    "engine": "knitr",
    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Data Collection Facts Label\"\nexecute:\n  format: html\n  echo: false\n  warning: false\n  message: false\n---\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\n<style>\ntable.nutrition-label {\n  width: 75%;\n  border-collapse: collapse;\n  border: 2px solid black;\n  font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n  font-size: 12px;\n  margin-left: auto;\n  margin-right: auto;\n}\n\ntable.nutrition-label th,\ntable.nutrition-label td {\n  border: 1px solid black;\n  padding: 5px 7px;\n}\n\ntable.nutrition-label thead tr:nth-child(2) {\n  display: none;\n}\n</style>\n<table class=\"nutrition-label\">\n <thead>\n<tr><th style=\"border-bottom:hidden;padding-bottom:0; padding-left:3px;padding-right:3px;text-align: center; font-weight: bold; color: white !important;padding-right: 4px; padding-left: 4px; background-color: black !important;font-size: 18px;\" colspan=\"2\"><div style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd; padding-bottom: 5px; \">Data Source Facts Label</div></th></tr>\n  <tr>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\">  </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\">  </th>\n  </tr>\n </thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \"> 1. Source Identity </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Source name </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> 2023 Rural–Urban Continuum Codes </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Domain/topic </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Rural–urban geography and county classification </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Source type </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Public government dataset </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;height: 26px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;height: 26px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \"> 2. Collection Context </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Collector/producer </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> U.S. Department of Agriculture, Economic Research Service </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Original purpose </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> The codes allow researchers, policy makers, and others to view county-level data by finer residential groups when analysing trends related to population density and metro influence. </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Collection method </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> The division of counties as either metro or nonmetro is based on the 2023 Office of Management and Budget delineation of metro areas. USDA ERS then uses Census population data and commuting data to divide counties into nine categories based on population size, urbanization, and proximity to metro areas. </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Record-creation event </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> A record gets created when USDA ERS classifies a county or county-equivalent during the 2023 Rural-Urban Continuum Codes update. </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;height: 26px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;height: 26px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \"> 3. Observation and Scope </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Unit of observation </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> A county or county-equivalent classified by its rural–urban characteristics. </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Population or objects represented </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> U.S. counties and county-equivalents, including those in U.S. territories. </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Time period covered </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> The 2023 classification is based on Census population data from 2020, American Community Survey commuting data from 2016–2020, and metropolitan area definitions from 2023. </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Geographic area coverage </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> The entirety of the US, including all US territories. </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;height: 26px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;height: 26px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \"> 4. Variables and Data Structure </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Main variables/fields </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> County FIPS code, State, County Name, 2020 Population, 2023 Rural Urban Continuum Code (RUCC) and a discription of the rural urban classification. </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Data types included </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> FIPS codes are currently stored as double (dbl), but I plan to convert them to character (chr) because they are identifiers rather than quantities. All remaining columns are stored as character (chr). </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Direct measurements </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> County population recorded in the 2020 Census (Population_2020) </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Possible proxy variables </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> RUCC_2023 can be used to see a county’s degree of rurality and metropolitan influence. </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;height: 26px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;height: 26px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \"> 5. Documentation </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Documentation found </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> The USDA ERS documentation page includes an overview, scope and coverage, methods, code definitions, strengths and limitations, and links to the original data sources. </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Stated collection details </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> USDA ERS used data from the 2023 OMB metropolitan classifications, 2020 Census, and American Community Survey commuting data from 2016 to 2020. </td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n",
